==German==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|de|bʰerǵʰ}}
From {{inh|de|goh|burg}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*burgz}}, from {{inh|de|ine-pro||*bʰérǵʰ-s}}, a form of {{inh|de|ine-pro|*bʰerǵʰ-||fortified elevation}}. Compare {{cog|nl|burcht}}, {{cog|en|borough}}, {{m|en|-bury|&#8209;bury}}, {{cog|da|borg}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/bʊʁk/|[bʊʁk]|[bʊɐ̯k]}} {{a|standard}}
* {{IPA|de|/bʊɐ̯ç/}} {{a|northern and central Germany; chiefly colloquial}}
* {{audio|de|De-Burg.ogg|Audio}}

